WEBVTT

00:00:31.116 --> 00:00:32.116
Thank you.

00:01:02.040 --> 00:01:05.600
Quest in O-Reptil

00:01:05.600 --> 00:01:12.590
Brazilian version BKS

00:01:13.280 --> 00:01:22.380
The only thing the radar captured this night was a satellite drug

00:01:22.380 --> 00:01:23.830
Do you want me to take it?

00:01:24.440 --> 00:01:26.400
Of course, if you can handle the emotion

00:01:32.940 --> 00:01:55.970
What is this? Let's go!

00:02:07.480 --> 00:02:08.120
What's going on?

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:10.270
Investigate that side. I'm going to the back.

00:02:24.150 --> 00:02:25.470
Central, come on. Let's go.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:33.790
What's going on?

00:02:33.890 --> 00:02:34.720
Watch out!

00:02:35.020 --> 00:02:45.100
How long will it take, Doctor?

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:46.520
A long time.

00:02:47.230 --> 00:02:50.590
He's obeying the return signal in record time.

00:02:52.840 --> 00:02:55.370
Dr. Forbes, the attack is already being reported.

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:57.780
The radar base was completely destroyed.

00:02:58.990 --> 00:02:59.880
And some...

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:01.680
about the person responsible for this.

00:03:02.880 --> 00:03:04.240
They have no clue.

00:03:06.710 --> 00:03:07.270
Excellent.

00:03:13.100 --> 00:03:15.460
You deserve congratulations, Doctor.

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:20.260
There's still a long way to go, Simon. This is just the beginning.

00:03:36.520 --> 00:03:40.400
A one-eighth mark with this angle? But it's impressive, Dr. Quest.

00:03:40.820 --> 00:03:42.400
That was just a sample, General.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:44.330
Quester 1 to Quester 2.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:48.530
Quester 1 to Quester 2. Ready for separation?

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:50.600
What does the crew say?

00:03:50.840 --> 00:03:54.320
We are ready. We were waiting for my father to ask, right, bandit?

00:03:56.690 --> 00:03:58.050
Very well, Race. In action.

00:03:58.510 --> 00:03:59.570
Quester 2...

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:11.660
But it's amazing, two jets in one.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:15.380
And if you think this jet will reach us, pay close attention.

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:24.360
It's our turn, Ray.

00:04:24.660 --> 00:04:27.100
Hold on, boys. Now we're going to fly in a spiral.

00:04:38.000 --> 00:04:40.440
Wow! And you want to explore the coast, don't you?

00:04:42.460 --> 00:04:45.840
All right, Bandit. The show is over. We gave the general an idea.

00:04:55.220 --> 00:04:58.020
This surpasses, without a doubt, everything we have at our disposal.

00:04:58.400 --> 00:04:59.760
You only saw manoeuvra-

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:04.900
Even your surveillance system rivals our spy planes?

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:07.100
Yes, but we use it only for research.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:10.760
This project is many years ahead of the original Jato Quest.

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:15.320
On Earth, there is probably no inaccessible place for a Quest aircraft.

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:19.340
That is precisely why you are here, Dr. Quest.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:23.300
I already doubted that your visit would only be a simple demonstration.

00:05:31.760 --> 00:05:34.240
The General has no idea who is responsible for the attacks?

00:05:35.120 --> 00:05:36.060
Apparently not.

00:05:36.590 --> 00:05:38.770
So far, three radar bases have been attacked.

00:05:39.130 --> 00:05:41.150
All of them on islands in the South Seas.

00:05:41.450 --> 00:05:43.190
The islands themselves have been fully examined.

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:46.310
And this leaves us with this triangular area between them.

00:05:46.670 --> 00:05:48.820
And where are we entering now?

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.560
What are we looking for exactly?

00:05:51.120 --> 00:05:53.840
A submarine, a ship, a submarine base, maybe?

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:54.600
I'm not sure.

00:05:55.690 --> 00:05:58.070
According to the maps, there's only ocean here.

00:05:58.410 --> 00:05:59.970
Hmm, I don't like the idea.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.240
What is that, Doctor? A dense cloud at sea level.

00:06:03.900 --> 00:06:05.400
Let's see what the sonar can show.

00:06:08.310 --> 00:06:09.510
Well, but this is...

00:06:09.510 --> 00:06:10.270
What is this?

00:06:11.130 --> 00:06:12.310
An island that is not on the map.

00:06:12.630 --> 00:06:13.890
Isn't it better to take a closer look?

00:06:30.480 --> 00:06:42.890
But what? But what was that?

00:06:43.310 --> 00:06:47.390
It seemed to be a pterodactyl, but with a... a brontosaurus head.

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:48.850
A flying nightmare, in my opinion.

00:06:49.980 --> 00:06:52.990
Hey, Johnny, look!

00:06:53.330 --> 00:06:56.580
Gee, Hadi, this looks like the land that time has forgotten.

00:06:57.000 --> 00:06:58.820
I think we should forget too.

00:07:21.240 --> 00:07:22.260
Not this time.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:25.530
But the only thing I want is a picture of that pterodactyl.

00:07:25.610 --> 00:07:26.310
Sorry, Johnny.

00:07:26.710 --> 00:07:28.530
First we will examine the place.

00:07:28.810 --> 00:07:29.630
You may need us.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:31.760
If we need to, we'll call the communicator.

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:32.970
But, but...

00:07:32.970 --> 00:07:38.280
Case closed. We'll be back in a few hours.

00:07:38.920 --> 00:07:51.140
I tried, Johnny. I was also upset for not going.

00:07:52.170 --> 00:07:53.730
Yeah, but the boat stayed here with us.

00:07:54.380 --> 00:07:55.500
You heard the orders.

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:57.300
And your adventure spirit, Hardy?

00:07:57.680 --> 00:07:59.300
We're just going out to try the boat.

00:08:02.430 --> 00:08:03.610
Let's go to a higher point.

00:08:18.750 --> 00:08:20.770
After all these years.

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:23.690
Simon, get the patch.

00:08:23.870 --> 00:08:26.430
You two are about to become a reception committee.

00:08:50.000 --> 00:08:59.880
I have no doubts, doctor. Another vehicle passed by.

00:09:00.840 --> 00:09:03.260
We are not the only ones on this island.

00:09:03.480 --> 00:09:06.360
It would be better to inform the general and leave it to the military.

00:09:07.560 --> 00:09:08.640
What is this?

00:09:08.780 --> 00:09:12.020
Oh my God!

00:09:12.180 --> 00:09:18.790
Is it a kind of dinosaur?

00:09:19.330 --> 00:09:20.890
Many species, I would say.

00:09:21.090 --> 00:09:22.570
It's a mutation in history.

00:09:22.890 --> 00:09:25.250
Like that flying reptile we saw.

00:09:34.340 --> 00:09:37.840
He's part Triceratops, part Dinosaur, part...

00:09:37.840 --> 00:09:42.800
I think we better get out of these parts.

00:09:43.160 --> 00:09:43.380
What?

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:48.660
Back off, monster!

00:09:49.160 --> 00:09:57.290
I think we have to thank him.

00:09:58.010 --> 00:09:59.690
Yeah, and it's very efficient.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.560
What is this weapon that you have there?

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:05.560
It is a tornado, specially designed to control these animals,

00:10:05.860 --> 00:10:08.120
as well as unwanted visitors.

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:18.310
I still don't see any sign of the Dactylons.

00:10:18.310 --> 00:10:21.310
Well, if it didn't show up, I've already taken some good pictures of the island.

00:10:22.240 --> 00:10:25.180
Look, Hadi, stand there, I'm going to take a picture of you.

00:10:25.440 --> 00:10:26.300
I think it's great, Johnny.

00:10:26.540 --> 00:10:28.820
Stay still while I fix the focus, okay?

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:38.200
Very well, Hadi. Look at the little bird.

00:10:38.810 --> 00:10:40.770
In my land, we look at the elephant.

00:10:51.060 --> 00:10:58.120
And this one is full of teeth!

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:09.460
It's ahead, Hattie! Look! The boat is going away!

00:11:09.840 --> 00:11:13.420
Yes, yes, Salabim! Yes, yes, Salabim!

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:27.600
Good job, Hattie! One day you'll have to teach me this trick!

00:11:34.530 --> 00:11:38.280
They're out of here!

00:11:41.310 --> 00:11:48.870
The others!

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:51.660
Yeah, let's go to the quest room now.

00:11:51.740 --> 00:11:59.080
Where are they taking us?

00:11:59.280 --> 00:11:59.820
To a meeting.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:03.240
I have a special opinion. Dr. Forbus is anxious to see you again.

00:12:04.000 --> 00:12:05.700
Forbus? The biochemist?

00:12:05.960 --> 00:12:08.640
I knew you'd remember that name.

00:12:09.060 --> 00:12:12.040
You were very kind to bring the means of transport.

00:12:20.450 --> 00:12:21.570
Emergency signal!

00:12:21.900 --> 00:12:23.680
Dr. Questerace is in danger!

00:12:24.200 --> 00:12:25.800
We're going in the wrong direction!

00:12:38.540 --> 00:12:40.740
I see you're back to your old tricks.

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:44.420
My experiences with hybrids are not tricks.

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:49.120
I have some things to show that your shy scientists never imagined they could do.

00:12:49.760 --> 00:12:52.770
I think we've already found some of your monsters.

00:12:53.170 --> 00:12:56.450
I don't need to worry about the presence of my animals here.

00:12:56.670 --> 00:12:59.230
This whole area is protected by a force field.

00:13:00.160 --> 00:13:01.520
Radio, my son, are you in danger?

00:13:01.930 --> 00:13:03.070
The afternoon is falling.

00:13:03.370 --> 00:13:06.670
Let's hope they have enough judgment to stay in the jet.

00:13:07.140 --> 00:13:09.540
Otherwise, they will be food for happy days.

00:13:10.860 --> 00:13:12.610
Are we far?

00:13:12.910 --> 00:13:15.150
A lot, but now they are stopped.

00:13:15.430 --> 00:13:15.730
Nado!

00:13:31.690 --> 00:13:32.960
Johnny, he got us!

00:13:37.350 --> 00:13:40.290
He's too strong! The spear doesn't want to get out of the place!

00:13:49.230 --> 00:13:50.250
Hiding trick, Rad!

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:56.340
Nice to meet you, Rad!

00:14:00.480 --> 00:14:11.490
I have no idea, Johnny.

00:14:11.770 --> 00:14:14.130
That light must have something to do with that.

00:14:14.370 --> 00:14:16.060
Maybe someone has called him.

00:14:18.250 --> 00:14:22.490
No doubt you must be wondering how I created my dinosaur hybrids.

00:14:22.750 --> 00:14:24.250
Yeah, that crossed my mind.

00:14:24.530 --> 00:14:28.750
They are clones taken directly from fossil dinosaur bone cells.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:33.920
I have returned life to dead creatures for millions of years.

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:38.310
I imagine that certain foreign powers would pay a lot for these secrets.

00:14:38.790 --> 00:14:42.210
And they will pay even more for my last creation.

00:14:43.830 --> 00:14:49.550
But in the name of heaven...

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:50.930
My reptilian is in front of you.

00:14:52.050 --> 00:14:57.330
The result of the combination of human bones and dinosaurs through my clone process.

00:14:57.590 --> 00:14:59.810
And I bet it was the toad here that attacked the...

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:05.450
Yes, to test your destructive potential and respond to commands.

00:15:05.950 --> 00:15:10.330
You know, he is the first, let's say, soldier of this kind.

00:15:10.830 --> 00:15:17.780
The same foreign powers will pay a fortune for an army of creatures so powerful.

00:15:18.200 --> 00:15:24.690
An army to which I will soon give life.

00:15:25.370 --> 00:15:28.360
Only a madman could create this.

00:15:30.220 --> 00:15:30.620
What are you doing, Doctor?

00:15:32.840 --> 00:15:33.840
Behind you!

00:15:35.660 --> 00:15:36.830
Get him!

00:15:39.830 --> 00:15:40.510
I'll get him!

00:15:41.220 --> 00:15:47.790
But that's great!

00:15:48.150 --> 00:15:52.460
That was really crazy, Mr. Bell.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:03.120
It looks like the swamp ends here. According to the communicators, they are up ahead.

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:08.900
It's time for the motorcycles!

00:16:09.480 --> 00:16:15.620
That's right, Hattie. You can jump, buddy.

00:16:17.400 --> 00:16:26.180
And we'll find him soon.

00:16:26.610 --> 00:16:28.830
Yeah, it looks like there are a lot of restless reptiles around here.

00:16:31.500 --> 00:16:34.250
Hey, slow down! I think I saw light over there.

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:40.840
Wow, look!

00:16:45.560 --> 00:16:48.520
The Tyrannosaurus hybrid seems to be pretty close, doesn't it?

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:53.060
He smells like good food miles away.

00:16:54.300 --> 00:16:57.480
Maybe he's smelling like two rats too.

00:16:57.900 --> 00:16:59.960
But you'll stay and the rats...

00:17:00.000 --> 00:17:00.660
They're all going to leave.

00:17:04.280 --> 00:17:06.200
Enjoy your meal, Mr. Bannon.

00:17:08.100 --> 00:17:08.740
Let's go, Raj.

00:17:11.760 --> 00:17:12.460
Hey, Ray!

00:17:13.060 --> 00:17:16.430
Johnny! Raj! Hurry up! I'm waiting for a guest for dinner.

00:17:16.980 --> 00:17:18.240
We're going to let you go in a second.

00:17:19.610 --> 00:17:21.590
Uh-oh! The guest arrived earlier.

00:17:22.110 --> 00:17:27.120
I'm almost there.

00:17:30.700 --> 00:17:33.750
Leave me here! Run to the back of the force field before it's too late!

00:17:33.950 --> 00:17:36.680
I can retarded!

00:17:37.220 --> 00:17:37.660
Catch!

00:17:52.380 --> 00:17:55.940
I have to think fast!

00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:01.820
Good job, little bird!

00:18:07.440 --> 00:18:09.110
Good job, Hadi!

00:18:09.370 --> 00:18:09.990
Let's go, Johnny!

00:18:10.310 --> 00:18:10.830
I'm already going!

00:18:17.490 --> 00:18:17.930
This way!

00:18:18.370 --> 00:18:25.020
Come on, we have to help Dr. Quest!

00:18:25.280 --> 00:18:25.800
And where is he?

00:18:26.020 --> 00:18:27.620
Hey, who were those men?

00:18:32.270 --> 00:18:37.090
You realize, of course, that I can not allow you to organize an expedition to look for you.

00:18:37.570 --> 00:18:38.670
And what do you intend to do?

00:18:39.010 --> 00:18:42.630
Unfortunately, your jet will have to suffer an accident, doctor.

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:46.920
Yes, a fall into the ocean many kilometers from here.

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:50.080
The authorities will conclude that everyone died.

00:18:50.600 --> 00:18:53.280
And they will have died, I guarantee you.

00:18:53.380 --> 00:18:55.290
What happened to the lights?

00:19:02.290 --> 00:19:08.380
What's going on?

00:19:09.740 --> 00:19:14.610
Dr. Forbes, Simon, look, the cables were cut.

00:19:15.110 --> 00:19:17.360
I found this near the generator.

00:19:17.680 --> 00:19:18.900
It couldn't have been Bannon.

00:19:19.060 --> 00:19:22.140
If the generator is off, we are without the force field.

00:19:22.400 --> 00:19:24.690
There must be a way to save Dr. Quest.

00:19:25.510 --> 00:19:27.630
Look, we have a visitor.

00:19:30.120 --> 00:19:35.630
It's one of your monsters!

00:19:36.110 --> 00:19:37.830
Quick, Simon, we have to stop him!

00:19:38.090 --> 00:19:41.470
The torturer can't find him!

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:47.880
I have to get out of here! I need to get out!

00:19:48.300 --> 00:19:50.140
Where is the torturer, you idiot?

00:19:50.800 --> 00:19:51.860
Dad, we're here!

00:19:54.290 --> 00:19:54.630
Johnny!

00:19:54.810 --> 00:19:55.920
In the square, Doctor!

00:19:57.010 --> 00:19:59.610
If he comes in, we're lost!

00:20:00.060 --> 00:20:11.020
I found it!

00:20:11.020 --> 00:20:11.400
God!

00:20:23.200 --> 00:20:24.900
Do you think they managed to get out?

00:20:25.180 --> 00:20:26.660
If they didn't get out, they're liquidated.

00:20:26.760 --> 00:20:29.970
Well, we examined every centimeter of the...

00:20:30.000 --> 00:20:31.760
and we didn't find any sign of anyone.

00:20:32.600 --> 00:20:33.520
It's a shame.

00:20:34.160 --> 00:20:35.740
Forbus had a brilliant mind.

00:20:36.020 --> 00:20:36.900
But a little strange.

00:20:37.260 --> 00:20:38.860
No, it was very strange.

00:20:39.660 --> 00:20:39.920
Huh?

00:20:40.180 --> 00:20:42.060
Hey, look!

00:20:43.480 --> 00:20:48.500
Watch out, bandit.

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:49.720
That thing can fly.

00:20:52.010 --> 00:20:52.950
He's disappearing.

00:20:53.810 --> 00:20:56.090
This is the biggest cloud I've ever seen in my life.

00:20:56.450 --> 00:20:59.730
It's the tomb of a mad scientist who had a dream.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:02.520
Sometimes we see, and then we don't see anymore.

00:21:02.950 --> 00:21:06.070
I think this is our way to go, right friends?

00:21:06.430 --> 00:21:06.790
Right!

00:21:15.000 --> 00:21:19.460
